From: Romain Tisserand <romain.tisserand@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid compilation issues with ncurses on GCC 15

ncurses built by GCC 15 (C23 by default) makes NCURSES_BOOL an int and
leaves NCURSES_ENABLE_STDBOOL_H at 0, so in htop (built as -std=c99)
curses.h redefines bool to int and CommandLine.c fails:

  passing argument 3 of 'MainPanel_updateLabels' makes integer from
  pointer without a cast [-Wint-conversion]

Upstream fixed it in 04d0a5456c87 by AC_DEFINE'ing
NCURSES_ENABLE_STDBOOL_H in configure.ac, but Buildroot does not
autoreconf htop, so that patch has no effect here. Define it in
ProvideCurses.h, before curses.h is included, instead.

Upstream: https://github.com/htop-dev/htop/commit/04d0a5456c87c6ce7a77bef18b26e4b6dbb05265
---
--- a/ProvideCurses.h
+++ b/ProvideCurses.h
@@ -10,6 +10,12 @@
 
 #include "config.h" // IWYU pragma: keep
 
+// Same as upstream 04d0a545 (configure.ac), without needing autoreconf:
+// make ncurses use <stdbool.h> so bool matches the C compiler's bool.
+#ifndef NCURSES_ENABLE_STDBOOL_H
+#define NCURSES_ENABLE_STDBOOL_H 1
+#endif
+
 // IWYU pragma: begin_exports
 
 #if defined(HAVE_NCURSESW_CURSES_H)
